---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/ui/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AICodingAgentJourney from '../../components/infooo/coding/AICodingAgentJourney';
import { infoooWorlds, infoooIdentity } from '../../data/infooo';
import { absoluteUrl, breadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/seo';
import { url } from '../../utils/url';
const world = infoooWorlds.find(item => item.id === 'world-004')!;
const context = { site: Astro.site!, base: import.meta.env.BASE_URL };
const canonical = absoluteUrl(`/infooo/${world.slug}`, context);
const related = infoooWorlds.filter(item => world.relatedWorlds?.includes(item.id) && item.status === 'published' && item.visibility === 'public');
---
<BaseLayout title={`${world.title} — How Coding Agents Work | Khizooology`} description={world.description} canonical={canonical} accentColor={infoooIdentity.color} accentColorLight={infoooIdentity.colorLight} ogImage={world.hero!.asset} ogImageAlt={world.preview!.alt} socialTitle={world.title} socialDescription={world.description} jsonLd={[
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: world.title, applicationCategory: 'EducationalApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any', url: canonical, description: world.description, isAccessibleForFree: true },
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', ...breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Infooo', path: '/infooo' }, { name: world.title, path: `/infooo/${world.slug}` }], context) },
]}>
  <div class="k-container coding-breadcrumb"><Breadcrumb crumbs={[{ label: 'Infooo', href: url('/infooo') }, { label: world.title }]} accentColor={infoooIdentity.color} /></div>
  <AICodingAgentJourney client:load world={world} />
  <section class="coding-context k-container" aria-labelledby="coding-context-title"><h2 id="coding-context-title">What happens between “do this” and “done”?</h2><p>An AI coding agent combines a language model with tools that can inspect a software project and act within its permissions. A modern coding agent may search relevant files, read surrounding code and project instructions, plan a focused change, edit and observe the results. Available tools and instruction policies differ between systems.</p><p>The core loop is observe → decide → act → observe result. A failed test gives new evidence: inspect the failure, repair the implementation and rerun. Type checks, lint, unit tests and a production build answer different questions. Desktop and mobile preview checks can reveal problems that compilation misses.</p><p>This world uses three curated tasks: add dark mode, fix an empty-cart crash and consolidate retry logic. Explore files, search, editor, terminal, tests, browser and diff; see context change; try eight failure scenarios and five challenges. The advanced dark-mode finale combines test feedback, a mobile regression, repair, scope review and a final evidence-based report.</p><p>Human approval matters when intent is ambiguous or an action is risky. More autonomy does not grant production permission. Tool outputs are observations, not instructions that can override governing rules. A good report names what changed, what was verified and remaining blockers.</p><p>Everything here is a static browser-only simulation. There are no live AI calls, private reasoning transcripts, uploads, arbitrary code execution or real shell commands.</p><nav aria-label="Related knowledge worlds">{related.map(item => <a href={url(`/infooo/${item.slug}`)}>{item.title} — follow the code into production →</a>)}<a href={url('/infooo')}>Explore all Infooo worlds →</a></nav></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.coding-breadcrumb{padding-top:1.5rem;max-width:var(--k-container-visual)}.coding-context{max-width:var(--k-container-wide);padding-bottom:3rem}.coding-context h2{font:800 1.4rem Poppins,sans-serif}.coding-context p{max-width:850px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--k-text-muted)}.coding-context nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1.5rem;margin-top:1.5rem}.coding-context a{color:var(--k-text);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px}</style>
